<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1529"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Juno<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Juno<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, December 01, 2004 - 3:22 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Interesting reading and some good points.  However, in all fairness, BTK did not rape his victims. <BR> <BR>&#34;Is it likely that BTK is stealing cars? Absolutely given that he has no problem with houses.&#34; <BR> <BR>That doesn&#39;t really to make sense to me, nor does <BR>&#34;He got tired? More like he did not like sitting around in his stolen car.&#34; <BR> <BR>He was waiting IN THE HOUSE not ouside in a stolen car. <BR> <BR>I also do not think we can conclude he was in prison.  Just because he did not claim victims publicly at the time does not mean he was not still killing.  Or perhaps he killed infrequently.  Until Vicki Wegerle was brought to public attention BY BTK....Who Knew?  We do know that he wasn/t in prison then, when prior maybe one would think he was. The point is--one cannot assume he was in prison twice for extended periods just because there were &#42;apparently&#42; no BTK murders. <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
